-- title:
--   Localization at a rational point as a power series quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $m,r$ be natural numbers, and let $g \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to K[x_1,\dots,x_m]$ be a family of polynomials in $m$ variables; write $I$ for the ideal generated by the range of $g$ and $A := K[x_1,\dots,x_m]/I$. Let $\mathfrak n \subset A$ be a maximal ideal such that the class of each variable $X_j$ modulo $I$ lies in $\mathfrak n$, and assume that the localization $A_{\mathfrak n}$ of $A$ at $\mathfrak n$ is finite as a $K$-module. Then there exists an isomorphism $e$ of $K$-algebras from $A_{\mathfrak n}$ onto the quotient of the formal power series ring $K[[x_1,\dots,x_m]]$ by the ideal generated by the images of the $g_i$ under the inclusion of polynomials into power series, and $e$ is the natural map in the following sense: for every polynomial $p \in K[x_1,\dots,x_m]$, the value of $e$ at the image of $p \bmod I$ under the structure map $A \to A_{\mathfrak n}$ equals the class of $p$, read as a power series, in $K[[x_1,\dots,x_m]]/(g_1,\dots,g_r)$.
--
--   This identifies the local ring of a zero-dimensional complete intersection at the origin, assumed finite over $K$, with the corresponding quotient of the power series ring, and records that the identification is the obvious one on polynomial classes. The compatibility with polynomial classes is what allows explicit elements such as Jacobian or Bezoutian classes to be transported across the isomorphism; it is used in the proof of [`Algebra.bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#Algebra.bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_isAlgClosed).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_exists_algEquiv_localization_atPrime_mvPowerSeries_quotient_apply_mk.lean

